    {
      "id": "e2b2c002-2222-4000-8000-00000000000a",
      "name": "Scope Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [220, -260],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Receive, not poll — deliberately\nARIE has no \"list leads by status\" endpoint today, and implementing a client-side discovery/retry loop here would duplicate backend concerns this task explicitly says n8n must not own. Call this webhook with `{\"lead_id\": \"...\"}` once you already know a decision finalized. If ARIE later adds e.g. `GET /leads?status=...`, swap the Webhook trigger for a Schedule Trigger against that endpoint — the rest of the chain (fetch -> filter finalized -> transform -> sink) is unchanged.\n\n**Auth (Productization M2B):** \"GET /leads/{id}\" authenticates with an ARIE organization API key via n8n's built-in \"Header Auth\" credential (name `Authorization`, value `Bearer <key>`). Mint a `leads:read`-scoped key with `python -m scripts.mint_api_key --label 'n8n outcome sync' --scopes leads:read`, create/select the credential named \"ARIE Outcome Sync API Key\" on that node, and paste the key in there. No X-Organization-Id header — API-key auth derives the organization from the key. \"POST Mock CRM Sink\" is unaffected: it targets n8n's own local webhook, not ARIE's API.",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 480
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e2b2c002-2222-4000-8000-00000000000b",
      "name": "Qualified Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1180, -180],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "`qualified`, the finalized-status set, and the permanently-failed set all restate the same vocabulary `arie.statemachine.transitions` defines once (QUALIFIED/REJECTED/FAILURE) and `v_pipeline_metrics.cost_per_qualified_lead` reads from — relabeling for the CRM shape, not a second decision made in a second language. `tests/unit/test_n8n_workflows.py` checks these literal lists against that module so the two can't drift apart again.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 340
      }
    }
  ],
